   "content": {
    "description": "Chemistry: Edexcel iGCSE Paper 2 - Half-Term HyperCram > Speed Sections > Principles of Chemistry",
    "topicNotes": "Paper Chromatography In paper chromatography, mixtures of soluble substances are separated. A solvent (mobile phase) is run through the mixture on paper (containing the stationary phase). Method Use a pencil to draw a horizontal line near the bottom of the chromatography paper. On this ‘start line’, put samples of known substances (A-D) alongside an unknown substance (X). Method cont. Place the paper in a beaker containing a small volume of solvent. You should make sure the substances are not in the solvent as this can cause the substances to dissolve into the solvent in the beaker. Method cont; 4. Wait for the solvent to travel to near the top of the paper. As the solvent travels up the chromatography paper, it picks up the substances being tested and carries them up the chromatography paper. Method cont. By comparing spots produced by X with those produced by A-D, it should be possible to identify the unknown substance by comparing it to the known substances. The components that travel furthest are highly soluble in the solvent. They are also minimally attracted to the chromatography paper. Chromatogram A chromatogram is produced in a chromatography experiment. We use these to identify compounds in mixtures by calculating Rf values. Rf values Rf = distance travelled by the substance &divide; distance travelled by the solvent The solvent Rf values depend on the solvent. We can learn more about the identity of the components by testing any references and the unknown mixture in a range of solvents. References A reference substance is a pure sample that's run alongside the unknown mixture. References are used to see if it's a component in the mixture. These substances provide valuable evidence, but not proof of what's in a substance.",
    "imageUrl": "seneca-image-cdn:///2019-03/bee827bd-4484-4189-ac1f-2af30c0dc5a4/Paper-chromatography-apparatus%20(1).png",
    "previewUrl": "/resource-discover/preview/resource/07fc58bf-2417-4e81-9949-798a063aa8c0",
    "contentUrl": "/classroom/course/02dc4b91-0ea2-4fbe-99d0-023cebf96074/section/07fc58bf-2417-4e81-9949-798a063aa8c0/session/start"
   }
